      "text": [
        " «أَمَّا إِذَا قَرَأَ فَنَعَمْ وَ أَمَّا إِذَا أَوْمَأَ بِوَجْهِهِ لِلسُّجُودِ فَلْيَكْشِفْهُ حَيْثُ مَا أَوْمَأَتْ بِهِ اَلدَّابَّةُ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1296 - Sa'id ibn Yasarasked Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) about a man performing the night prayer while on his mount.\nHe asked: \"Is it permissible for him to cover his face while praying?\"\nHe (as) replied: \"Yes, when he is reciting (the Qur'an). However, when he gestures with his face for prostration, he should uncover it wherever the mount takes him”."
        ]
      }
